  {title:'Cations on the left',narration:'With element-type coloring and the slider on group 1, the highlighted column shows every alkali metal as a +1 cation; group 2 is +2. The positive charge simply equals the group number because these metals lose their outer electrons.',state:{groupSweep:1,colorScheme:false}},
