    },
    {
      "id": "elementCell",
      "type": "click",
      "teaches": "Selecting one cell reveals that element's specific ion charge, its electron configuration, and the group-trend rule that explains the charge — showing the charge is just the count of electrons lost or gained to reach a stable (often noble-gas) configuration"
